.intentfold/charter/operations.md:62:## Tools
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-63-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-64-**Production**
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-65-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-66-- Live URL: `https://lemmadeck.com`; `www` redirects to the apex.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-67-- Render origin: `https://lemmadeck.onrender.com`.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-68-- Workspace: `intentplex` (`tea-d229rofdiees73d7h4gg`).
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-69-- Web service: `lemmadeck` (`srv-dapsio9srm7s73an5p60`), Frankfurt, one `0.5c-512mb` instance.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-70-- GitHub repository: `wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck`, branch `main`, `autoDeploy=no`.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-71-- Health endpoint: `/healthz`, requiring session configuration and the existing Supabase connection;
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-72-  its response reports the deployed `RENDER_GIT_COMMIT`.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-73-- Cloudflare apex and `www`: DNS-only CNAMEs to `lemmadeck.onrender.com`, TTL 300.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-74-  Both custom domains are verified by Render, which provides TLS and the `www` redirect.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-75-- No Render database, disk, worker, cron, autoscaling, or preview service.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-76-- Retired domains `mynatree.com` and `stemrobin.com` serve nothing; their Cloudflare zones remain.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-77-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-78-**Install**
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-79-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-80-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-81-cd app && npm install
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-82-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-83-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-84-The content skills install separately:
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-85-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-86-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-87-npm --prefix .agents/skills install
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-88-npm --prefix .claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson install
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-89-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-90-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-91-`ld-s10y-lesson` also owns a Python virtual environment; its `SKILL.md` contains the exact `uv`
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-92-bootstrap command and required packages.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-93-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-94-**Run locally**
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-95-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-96-The fixed main port is recorded in `.intentfold/project.json` and set in `app/vite.config.ts`. Do not
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-97-pass `--port` in the main checkout:
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-98-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-99-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-100-cd app && npm run dev
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-101-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-102-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-103-For a ticket worktree, resolve the port and pass it to Vite:
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-104-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-105-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-106-python3 <intentfold-skill>/scripts/ports.py .intentfold/project.json ticket <ticket-id>
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-107-cd app && npm run dev -- --port <resolved-web-port>
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-108-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-109-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-110-**Build and tests**
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-111-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-112-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-113-cd app && npm run build
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-114-cd app && npm run start
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-115-cd app && npm run test
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-116-cd app && npm run e2e
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-117-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-118-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-119-The combined mechanical-defence command is in `engineering.md`.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-120-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-121-**Acceptance**
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-122-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-123-Use the Playwright copy installed in `app/`; do not install a second copy at the repo root. After a
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-124-fresh clone or upgrade:
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-125-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-126-```bash
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-127-cd app && npx playwright install chromium
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-128-```
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-129-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-130-Run a ticket-scoped `.mjs` check from `app/` so it resolves the existing Playwright package:
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-131-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-132-```bash
--
.intentfold/charter/operations.md:274:## Redlines
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-275-
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-276-1. **Recording a criterion as passed when its check did not run** — forbidden outright. An
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-277-   environment or external limit that stopped the run is recorded exactly as it happened.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-278-2. **Writing to the real learner's data from a test** — forbidden outright. Tests use
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-279-   `sr_users.id = 2`, never `sr_users.id = 1`.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-280-3. **Driving `https://lemmadeck.com` during acceptance** — forbidden outright. Signing in, clicking,
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-281-   submitting, or any other write-capable interaction is prohibited; acceptance runs against
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-282-   localhost. A read-only GET required by the post-deploy check is allowed.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-283-4. **Writing a real password, session secret, or DB connection string into a check script, ticket
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-284-   artifact, or Charter file** — forbidden outright.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-285-5. **Running a destructive statement against `$LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`** — `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, or an
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-286-   unfiltered `DELETE`/`UPDATE` on any `sr_*` table — not without the human's explicit approval.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-287-6. **Creating or deleting cloud resources** — not without the human's explicit approval. Routine
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-288-   Render releases update only the existing approved service.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-289-7. **Deploying for the first time** — not without the human's explicit approval.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-290-8. **A deploy that changes more than the image's application code** — not without the human's
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-291-   explicit approval. This includes a schema statement run against the live database; a root
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-292-   `Dockerfile` or `infra/` change; a required environment key the container does not already have;
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-293-   or an ingress or scaling configuration change. Editing the descriptive DDL file without applying
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-294-   a schema statement is not itself a runtime change.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-295-9. **Moving the root `Dockerfile`, or changing its build context away from the repo root** —
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-296-   forbidden outright.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-297-10. **Allowing the production web service to scale to zero or sleep when idle** — forbidden
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-298-    outright; retain the always-on single-instance baseline.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-299-11. **Pointing a production domain at anything new, or changing the `lemmadeck.com` Cloudflare
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-300-    records or proxy state** — not without the human's explicit approval.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-301-12. **Reporting a deploy as done without running the post-deploy check** — forbidden outright.
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-302-13. **Any action incurring new recurring cost, or a one-off cost above $5** — not without the
.intentfold/charter/operations.md-303-    human's explicit approval.
--
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:92:## Tools
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-93-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-94-**Pull-request landing**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-95-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-96-Worktree tickets land through GitHub pull requests in `wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck`. Substitute the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-97-ticket's recorded values for `<ticket-id>`, `<branch>`, and `<pr>`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-98-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-99-Find an existing PR:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-100-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-101-```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-102-gh pr list --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --head <branch> --state all \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-103-  --json number,title,url,state,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-104-```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-105-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-106-Create one when absent:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-107-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-108-```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-109-gh pr create --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --base main --head <branch> \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-110-  --title "<ticket-id>" --body-file ".intentfold/tickets/<ticket-id>/handoff.md"
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-111-```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-112-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-113-Read its current head, state, and checks:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-114-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-115-```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-116-gh pr view <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-117-  --json number,url,state,headRefOid,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-118-```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-119-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-120-This repository currently configures no required GitHub checks, branch protection, rulesets,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-121-overlap detector, or cap4 takeover gate. If that changes, update these Tools before landing the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-122-next ticket. Merge with a merge commit, then confirm GitHub reports the merge commit:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-123-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-124-```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-125-gh pr merge <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --merge
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-126-gh pr view <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-127-```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-128-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-129-Do not pass `--delete-branch`; IntentFold cap4 deletes the local and remote ticket branches only
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-130-after the ticket backend reaches Done.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-131-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-132-**Mechanical defence**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-133-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-134-Run once before handoff:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-135-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-136-```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-137-python3 ssot-resources/audit.py
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-138-python3 ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/validate.py
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-139-node --test .agents/skills/lib/content-db.test.mjs
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-140-cd app && npm run test && npm run build
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-141-```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-142-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-143-There is no separate lint or typecheck script today; `vite build` is the type-error boundary.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-144-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-145-**Architecture and generation**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-146-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-147-- Build output: `app/.output` (`app/.output/server/index.mjs`).
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-148-- Content generation: never hand-write `sr_*` rows. Math starts at
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-149-  `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md`, delegates modern figures to `ld-s10y-image`, delegates
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-150-  answers and interaction specifications to `ld-s10y-answer`, and persists only through those
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-151-  skills' publishers. Its original scans, TOCs and durable artifacts live under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-152-  `ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/`; its renders, templates and previews live under `.tmp/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-153-  Biographies use `sr-story`; retained short-literature English generation uses `sr-voa1500` but
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-154-  does not publish a learner-facing application surface.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-155-  Each skill's `SKILL.md` owns its exact generation and persistence commands.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-156-- DB schema: `ssot-schemas/db-schemas/lemmadeck.sql` describes the live schema. It is generated from
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-157-  the database, never hand-edited and never applied to it. The inspection command lives in
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-158-  `operations.md`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-159-- `.agents/skills/lib/content-db.mjs` owns DB URL resolution for content scripts under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-160-  `.agents/skills/`. Repository-local S10Y publishers live under `.claude/skills/`, read the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-161-  repo-root `.env`, and must write through `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-162-- `app/src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by the TanStack Start plugin and is never hand-edited.
--
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:208:## Redlines
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-209-
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-210-1. **Committing credentials, tokens, connection strings, or hidden account data** — forbidden
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-211-   outright, in source, mocks, ticket artifacts, and commits alike. Concretely: `.env` and `app/.env`
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-212-   never appear in `git status`'s staged set.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-213-2. **Discarding a change already present in a dirty worktree** — forbidden outright. It is the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-214-   human's work until they say otherwise.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-215-3. **Sending an answer key to the client** — forbidden outright. The quiz question fetchers
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-216-   (`getLessonQuestions` / `getStoryQuestions` in `app/src/lib/quiz.ts`) must never include
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-217-   `correct_index`, `answer`, or `accept` in what they return; correctness is judged server-side in
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-218-   the `record*` server functions.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-219-4. **Opening a database connection anywhere under `app/` other than `app/src/lib/db.ts`** —
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-220-   forbidden outright. A second `postgres` client, or a connection string reaching any file under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-221-   `app/src/routes/` or any `.tsx`, is the crossing this names. Content scripts under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-222-   `.agents/skills/` are node CLIs governed by entry 9.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-223-5. **Adding, removing, or changing a dependency** — not without the human's explicit approval, and
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-224-   only when a ticket carries that decision.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-225-6. **Hand-editing a generated file** — forbidden outright: `app/src/routeTree.gen.ts`, anything under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-226-   `app/.output/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-227-7. **Changing the DB schema anywhere other than `ssot-schemas/db-schemas/lemmadeck.sql`** —
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-228-   forbidden outright. Ad hoc `ALTER`/`CREATE` against the shared server is drift.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-229-8. **Using a database connection other than `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL` for application or content
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-230-   access** — forbidden outright. `DATABASE_URL` and `EASYAPP_DATABASE_URL` are not aliases;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-231-   same-named schemas on other servers are not the product database.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-232-9. **A content script under `.agents/skills/` calling `postgres(` directly** — forbidden outright.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-233-   Every content script connects through `.agents/skills/lib/content-db.mjs`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-234-10. **Adding a repo-root `package.json`, or a second application** — not without the human's explicit
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-235-    approval. The standalone-`app/` layout is what the root `Dockerfile` builds.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-236-11. **Committing a product resource outside `ssot-resources/`, or making durable content depend on
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-237-    `.tmp/`** — forbidden outright. Code-owned schemas, profiles, dependency files and test fixtures
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md-238-    remain beside code. `python3 ssot-resources/audit.py` is the mechanical boundary.
--
